    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"The team has lending counts, return times, and guest comments from one gathering.\", \"decision\": \"How should the pilot choose its next change?\", \"goal\": \"Make cup lending and return convenient while keeping the available stock and volunteer work understandable.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood café wants to lend reusable cups at community gatherings and recover them afterward. It has a modest cup stock, washable collection crates, a simple lending record, and volunteers who can share short shifts. The plan concerns a small pilot with no deposit or sales system. Different decisions address separate moments in lending, return, and review.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe team starts with the slowest return times and checks guest comments before choosing a change. The next trial addresses a delay with an explanation from guests.\nThe team starts with the most common guest comment and checks lending counts and return times before choosing a change. The next trial addresses a reported difficulty supported by usage records.\nThe team proposes one change and compares its likely effect against lending counts, return times, and guest comments. The next trial follows a proposal checked against all three records."
    }
